Responsible Use Notice

This project is published for educational and authorized security-research
purposes only (e.g. CTFs, coursework, and testing networks/devices you own
or have explicit written permission to test).

Wi-Fi deauthentication, rogue AP / evil-twin, and beacon-flooding techniques
can disrupt networks and, depending on your jurisdiction, using them against
networks or devices without the owner's consent may be illegal (in the
United States this can fall under the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act and FCC
regulations on RF interference; equivalent laws exist in most other
countries). The authors of this project accept no responsibility for misuse.
If you didn't build the network, ask before you test it.
